pper_adhesion_shape_retention_texture_acceptability_consumption_packaging_waste_and_cooling_burden_thresholds","treat_trial_results_as_local_to_the_tested_lot_route_bag_position_weather_and_duration_not_a_universal_brand_winner","choose_only_the_lowest_total_trip_cost_and_carry_burden_exact_path_that_passes_current_label_safety_packaging_and_matched_route_exposure_gates_otherwise_use_a_proven_control_or_defer"],"scenario":"A summer bike commuter and weekend hiker wants sweet snacks that can ride through a roughly 90-degree afternoon without becoming a leaking, wrapper-stuck mess. Four frozen seller pages show an M&M'S 38-ounce milk-chocolate party bag at 11.79 dollars rated 73 percent over twelve reviews, a 29.99-dollar Skittles tub described as ninety individually wrapped fun-size packets with no posted review, a 7.96-dollar thirteen-ounce Jolly Rancher sour hard-candy bag rated 85 percent over twelve reviews, and a 19.95-dollar six-count Charleston Chew selection described as 1.87-ounce nougat bars with a chocolatey coating and no posted review. The pages describe form, packaging, price and seller wording but do not report a controlled 90-degree pannier or backpack trial, exact melting or glass-transition thresholds, complete current physical labels for every offer, or route-specific safety. General pages define melting point, crystal polymorphism, compound chocolate, hard candy, glass transition, hygroscopy, ice packs and shelf-stable food. Community pages describe one sweat-sogged paper-wrapped candy after a workout, one old large cooler said to stay cold with ice, and a disputed salt-and-ice cooler explanation. None identifies the exact four products under a matched route, bag, exposure, humidity and packaging protocol.","target":"Determine what the four frozen seller pages actually establish about price, rating sample, pack, mass, form and packaging, and whether any source proves that an exact snack survives a roughly 90-degree pannier or hiking-pack route. Explain the distinct and limited roles of crystalline melting, polymorphism, compound coating, hard-candy glass transition, humidity uptake, shelf-stable storage and portable cooling without assigning unsupported product thresholds. Keep the three community examples at their exact anecdotal scope. End with a current-label and seal checklist, measurement of the actual bag exposure, a small matched leakproof route trial with cooling treated separately, predeclared mess, texture, waste and burden criteria, and a selection procedure that selects only a passing exact path, uses a proven control, or defers."},"graph_motif":"multi_branch_synthesis","graph_node_to_step_id":{"bridge_chocolate_phase_and_coating_boundary":"B1","bridge_current_label_safety_route_gate":"B5","bridge_exact_offer_heat_form_matrix":"B2","bridge_matched_hot_route_portability_trial":"B6","bridge_sugar_glass_humidity_boundary":"B3","bridge_transport_cooling_exposure_boundary":"B4","decision_evidence_bounded_hot_weather_snack_choice":"D1","prop_charleston_chew_coating_scope":"E1","prop_compound_chocolate_scope":"E2","prop_crystal_polymorphism_scope":"E3","prop_glass_transition_scope":"E4","prop_hard_candy_formulation_scope":"E5","prop_hygroscopy_scope":"E6","prop_ice_pack_exposure_scope":"E7","prop_jolly_rancher_hard_offer_scope":"E8","prop_melting_point_scope":"E9","prop_mms_offer_shell_scope":"E10","prop_old_cooler_anecdote_scope":"E11","prop_salt_ice_discussion_scope":"E12","prop_shelf_stable_scope":"E13","prop_skittles_packet_offer_scope":"E14","prop_sweat_wrapper_anecdote_scope":"E15"},"motif_compilation_schema":"graph_motif_compilation_v1","topology_checks":{"has_multiple_independent_branches":true,"has_synthesized_decision":true}},"directly_scorable_gold":false,"discovery_parameters":{"max_expansion_depth":6,"per_stratum":4,"selection_seed":"50"},"graph_stamp":"evidence-graph-v1:sha256:40bef010c51f414ca98f588a900a72717c6d64c276afbc0dd48f064694ad7f4b","schema":"motif_candidate_compilation_bundle_v1"